      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.03,
      "end_seconds": 8.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.87,
      "end_seconds": 15.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "tell me what's brought you in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.35,
      "end_seconds": 25.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "honestly, it's a sore on the bottom of my foot, and my family pushed me to come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.89,
      "end_seconds": 33.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.31,
      "end_seconds": 39.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "actually, it's been like this since last Tuesday"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.83,
      "end_seconds": 50.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.58,
      "end_seconds": 55.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "I'd say moderate. Walking definitely sets it off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.19,
      "end_seconds": 59.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.41,
      "end_seconds": 79.27,
      "duration_seconds": 17.86,
      "text": "Numbness in my feet goes along with it, most of the time ah, as for Numbness in my feet, I honestly can't say when that began it might have been last month or the month before"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.37,
      "end_seconds": 86.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "And what about confusion, calf pain, chest pain or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.45,
      "end_seconds": 92.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "No confusion, calf pain, chest pain or vomiting, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.74,
      "end_seconds": 95.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "What about black toes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.02,
      "end_seconds": 98.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "no, no black toes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.5,
      "end_seconds": 106.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.19,
      "end_seconds": 110.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Mm, no, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.21,
      "end_seconds": 129.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Alright, which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.46,
      "end_seconds": 134.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "It's glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.08,
      "end_seconds": 138.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.09,
      "end_seconds": 143.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.53,
      "end_seconds": 147.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.22,
      "end_seconds": 151.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.5,
      "end_seconds": 155.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.27,
      "end_seconds": 166.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "I had an operation for a hernia last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.02,
      "end_seconds": 179.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.91,
      "end_seconds": 183.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Diabetes, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.24,
      "end_seconds": 185.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 185.84,
      "end_seconds": 201.66,
      "duration_seconds": 15.82,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier. BMI works out to 23.1, heart rate 103, saturation 95 percent. Height 174 centimetres, BP is 109 over 69, weight 70 kilos, temperature is 38.2 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.61,
      "end_seconds": 204.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.19,
      "end_seconds": 222.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "I think blood tests makes sense here, for infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.15,
      "end_seconds": 224.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "that makes sense"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.1,
      "end_seconds": 247.89,
      "duration_seconds": 20.79,
      "text": "I think a foot X-ray makes sense here, for ulcer i'd like to arrange a swab from the ulcer for infected ulcer let's use amoxicillin/clavulanic acid, 625 milligrams, three times a day, for seven days you take it by mouth it's for foot infection"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.38,
      "end_seconds": 252.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.9,
      "end_seconds": 280.29,
      "duration_seconds": 25.39,
      "text": "keep the weight off that foot and keep the dressing dry try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit let's get you seen by the foot clinic, I'll arrange the letter come back or go to emergency straight away if the redness spreads or you feel unwell with a fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.23,
      "end_seconds": 288.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Okay, um, makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.33,
      "end_seconds": 301.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the swab result. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.85,
      "end_seconds": 306.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "okay, so thank you, doctor, goodbye"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.88,
      "end_seconds": 310.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
